// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-048
=adr: 048
=title: License-Based Module Activation
=date: 2026-03-30
=status: accepted

#ctx
Client pricing model: customers pay for optional modules.
Two modules: combustion_dl (Cloud/On-Prem DL analytics) | be_agent (Agentic AI Framework).
Single Docker image shipped to all customers; module control must not require image rebuild.
Client generates keys; customers cannot forge keys.
Layer model: physical+be_sense+outputs always | be_agent+cloud_on_prem conditional.
overviewDataFlow + platformArchitecture widgets render only licensed layers.

#opts
opt1: env var flags — customer can self-enable; no tamper resistance
opt2: HS256 JWT (symmetric) — LICENSE_SECRET shared generator↔platform; pragmatic for MVP
opt3: RS256 JWT (asymmetric) — private key at client only, public key baked in image; production-grade

#decision
MVP: HS256 JWT. LICENSE_SECRET baked into Docker image at build (ARG LICENSE_SECRET in Dockerfile).
Customer receives: Docker image + LICENSE_KEY string in .env. Cannot forge without LICENSE_SECRET.
Backend: LicenseService singleton — init() verifies JWT on startup, stores {valid,customer,modules[],expiresAt}.
Route: GET /api/v1/license (public, no auth) → returns license state. Frontend is never the authority.
Dev override: NODE_ENV=development + LICENSE_KEY absent → all modules enabled, customer='development'.
Upgrade path: replace HS256 with RS256; swap LICENSE_SECRET for LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY in config.

#consequences
+ Single image for all customers; upgrade = new LICENSE_KEY string + container restart only
+ Client generates keys independently using generator CLI (private repo, not shipped to customers)
+ exp claim supports subscription/annual licensing with renewal warnings in UI
- HS256: LICENSE_SECRET must remain secret; if leaked, keys can be forged (RS256 upgrade resolves)
- Module UI code still bundled in image (gating is render-time, not build-time tree-shaking)
- New constraint: frontend MUST NOT self-decide module availability; always reads /api/v1/license

#scope
~arch_summary_update: yes
~new_backend: LicenseService, LicenseController, license.routes
~new_frontend: licenseSlice, useLicense hook
~affected: KosmosShell, WidgetPalette, overviewDataFlow, KosmosArchitectureTabPanel
~new_devices: combustion_ml_engine (combustion_dl module), be_sense_edge (be_agent module)
~docker: add NATS + Redis to docker-compose.yml + docker-compose.dev.yml (previously missing)
~gap: GAP-L1 = license generator CLI in separate private repo (not platform repo)
